-- title:
--   Generators of K ⊗_P IP and vanishing on J· I
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $n$ a natural number, and write $P_0 = R[x_0,\dots,x_{n-1}]$ for the polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R`. Let $M$ be a submonoid of $P_0$ and let $P$ be a commutative $P_0$-algebra that is a localisation of $P_0$ at $M$. Let $I$ and $J$ be ideals of $P_0$, and let $\mathfrak a$ be an ideal of $P$ assumed equal to the image ideal $I\,P = I.\mathrm{map}(P_0 \to P)$. Let $K$ be a commutative ring that is both a $P$-algebra and a $P_0$-algebra, compatibly (the scalar tower $P_0 \to P \to K$), such that the structure map $P_0 \to K$ is surjective and annihilates $J$, i.e. $j \mapsto 0$ in $K$ for every $j \in J$. The conclusion is a conjunction about the $K$-module $K \otimes_P \mathfrak a$, where $\mathfrak a$ is viewed as a $P$-module: first, every element $z$ of $K \otimes_P \mathfrak a$ can be written as $z = c \cdot (1 \otimes a)$ for some $c \in K$ and some $a \in I$, where $a$ is regarded as the element $\mathrm{algebraMap}(a)$ of $\mathfrak a$; second, for every $a$ in the product ideal $J \cdot I$, the element $1 \otimes a$ of $K \otimes_P \mathfrak a$ is zero, $a$ again being viewed in $\mathfrak a$ via its image in $P$.
--
--   This is a computation of the conormal-type module $K \otimes_P IP$ for a localisation $P$ of a polynomial ring and a quotient $K$ of $P$ killing $J$: it says the module is generated by a single element coming from $I$ and that elements of $J \cdot I$ contribute nothing. It is used in the verification of formal smoothness of localisations of quotients of polynomial rings at a prime under a condition on partial derivatives, via [`MvPolynomial.formallySmooth_localization_atPrime_quotient_of_forall_pderiv_mem`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.formallySmooth_localization_atPrime_quotient_of_forall_pderiv_mem).
